<Project>

  <!--
    Package identity for the two projects a plugin builds against. Everything else in the solution
    inherits these harmlessly, because only KHost.Abstractions and KHost.Common set IsPackable.

    The version here is the *contract* version, and it is not PluginApi.CurrentVersion. That one is
    the runtime gate the host checks a manifest against and moves only on a break; this one moves
    whenever the shape a plugin author compiles against changes at all, additions included. Keeping
    them apart is the point: an author needs to know their source will still compile, which a
    number that only ever counts breaks cannot tell them.

    0.x on purpose. The contracts still move under people — ScreenQrCode changed shape twice in one
    day — and a 1.0 would promise otherwise.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <ContractsVersion>0.29.0</ContractsVersion>
    <!--
      The assembly version is pinned and the package version is not, because they answer to
      different people. A plugin's compiled reference binds to this number, so moving it makes
      every plugin already in the wild fail to load — which is exactly what happened the first time
      these were packed: KHost.Plugins.Spotify bound to 1.0.0.0, the host served 0.1.0.0, and its
      break-music provider silently vanished with one line in the log.

      So it does not move at all, and has not since: PluginApi.CurrentVersion has gone 1 to 2 to 3
      while this stayed 1.0.0.0 on purpose. That number is the host's real compatibility gate, and
      it is checked against a manifest before a single assembly is bound, so an incompatible plugin
      is refused with a message a host can act on rather than failing to load for a reason nobody
      can read. Moving this as well would only replace that message with the outage above.
      ContractsVersion goes on the package and the file version, where it tells an author what they
      are compiling against without breaking anything already built.
    -->
    <AssemblyVersion>1.0.0.0</AssemblyVersion>
    <FileVersion>$(ContractsVersion).0</FileVersion>
    <Authors>Michael Riddle</Authors>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/riddlemd/KHost</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
